[center][url=https://bg3mm-redux.com/][b]Website[/b][/url] • [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux][b]GitHub & Documentation[/b][/url] • [url=https://discord.gg/rJJF89vqFZ][b]Discord[/b][/url][/center]
[left]

[/left]
[left]A community fork of [url=https://github.com/LaughingLeader/BG3ModManager]LaughingLeader's BG3 Mod Manager[/url], with a redesigned interface and a much larger set of tools for organizing and managing BG3 mods.[/left]
[center][/center]
[quote][color=#F0B44D][b]Redux is currently in public alpha.[/b][/color]

Redux has been developed and maintained primarily by me over the past few months. The core workflows have had a lot of testing, but I could not realistically cover every mod setup or Windows configuration.[b]Bugs should still be expected.[/b]

If you find something, the quickest way to get it in front of me is to [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/issues][b]open a GitHub issue[/b][/url] or [url=https://discord.gg/rJJF89vqFZ][b]join the Redux Discord[/b][/url]. Clear reproduction steps and screenshots are especially useful.

Keep backups of important saves, profiles, saved orders, downloaded packages, your BG3 Mods folder, and [i]modsettings.lsx[/i] while Redux is in alpha.[/quote]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/01-what-is-redux.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Redux keeps the familiar [b]Active Mods[/b], [b]Inactive Mods[/b], and [b]Override Mods[/b] workflow from BG3 Mod Manager, while adding a broader set of tools around it.

The goal has been to make large mod setups easier to organize, inspect, recover, and maintain without replacing the parts of BG3MM that already work well.

Redux adds categories, separators, load-order history and comparison, downloads, save management, diagnostics, native-package handling, custom themes, accessibility options, and a lot of smaller workflow improvements.

Important actions also stay separate:

[list]
[*]Downloading does not automatically install.[/*]
[*]Installing a normal PAK does not automatically activate it.[/*]
[*]Editing a load order does not automatically save it.[/*]
[*]Saving a Redux order does not automatically sync it to Baldur's Gate 3.[/*]
[/list]

Redux is meant to give you more information and better tools without quietly making those decisions for you.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/02-main-features.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Categories[/b] — custom names, colors, icons, descriptions, filters, ordering, and multiple categories per mod.[/*]
[*][b]Separators[/b] — named, colored, collapsible sections directly inside Active Mods.[/*]
[*][b]Selected Mod Drawer[/b] — descriptions, requirements, files, changelogs, diagnostics, source information, and personal notes without leaving the main window.[/*]
[*][b]Load Order Tools[/b] — saved-order comparison, history, restore points, and supported Undo/Redo.[/*]
[*][b]Download Manager[/b] — local packages and optional Nexus Mod Manager downloads in one persistent inbox.[/*]
[*][b]Package Archive Library[/b] — optional retention of verified install packages for later reuse.[/*]
[*][b]Save Game Manager[/b] — campaign grouping, thumbnails and metadata where available, imports, and safer deletion.[/*]
[*][b]Game-Directory Mod Manager[/b] — guarded support for a reviewed set of Script Extender, native, and root-level package layouts.[/*]
[*][b]Mod Diagnostics[/b] — read-only information for dependencies, conflicts, UUID issues, Script Extender requirements, overrides, and other detectable package conditions.[/*]
[*][b]Load Order Advisor[/b] — optional experimental guidance with a preview before any changes are applied.[/*]
[*][b]Themes & Accessibility[/b] — Redux Dark, Redux Light, Parchment, custom themes, imported fonts, text sizing, Reduce Motion, configurable shortcuts, background controls, and more.[/*]
[/list]

Redux has grown beyond what makes sense to document fully on a Nexus page.

For the [b]complete feature list, installation and update documentation, troubleshooting, privacy information, developer tools, release notes, and technical details[/b], see the [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux][b]GitHub repository[/b][/url].


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/03-organization.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Categories and separators are Redux-only organization tools.

Categories can be used for filtering and grouping without affecting the real BG3 load order.

Separators create persistent sections inside Active Mods and can be collapsed without changing the mods contained within them.

[b]Categories, separators, colors, icons, and notes are never written into [i]modsettings.lsx[/i].[/b]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/04-saving-and-syncing.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Redux treats the order you are currently editing, the Redux order you have saved, and the order currently written to BG3 as separate states.

[b]Save[/b] updates your selected Redux saved order.

[b]Sync Load Order to Game[/b] separately previews and writes the reviewed order to Baldur's Gate 3.

Load Order History, restore points, supported Undo/Redo, and external-change protection are there to make experimentation easier to recover from.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/05-downloads.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Download Manager acts as a persistent inbox for supported local packages and optional Nexus Mod Manager links.

Redux inspects packages before routing them to the appropriate workflow:

[list]
[*]Normal PAK mods are installed to [b]Inactive Mods[/b].[/*]
[*]Save packages are handled by [b]Save Game Manager[/b].[/*]
[*]Reviewed Script Extender, native, and root-level packages use [b]Game-Directory Mod Manager[/b].[/*]
[/list]

Installing a normal PAK does not automatically activate, reorder, save, or sync it.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/06-save-game-manager.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Save Game Manager groups saves by campaign and can show thumbnails, dates, sizes, and difficulty information when that metadata is available.

It supports staged imports from save folders, loose [i].lsv[/i] files, and supported archives.

Existing names require confirmation before replacement, and normal deletions use the Windows Recycle Bin.

[b]Redux does not edit or repair save contents.[/b]

Close BG3 before modifying saves, and keep independent backups.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/07-game-directory-mods.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Native and root-level mods are kept separate from ordinary PAK installation.

Game-Directory Mod Manager supports a limited set of reviewed package layouts and shows the intended destination before applying changes.

Unknown or unsupported native layouts remain blocked instead of being guessed into place.

[quote]
A recognized layout does not mean a DLL has been malware-scanned, publisher-verified, or guaranteed compatible.

Native DLLs execute inside the game. Only install native code from sources you trust.[/quote]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/08-diagnostics-and-load-order-advisor.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

[b]Mod Diagnostics[/b] is read-only and surfaces information Redux can detect locally.

The [b]Load Order Advisor[/b] is a separate, optional, experimental feature. It can propose an [b]Organize Active Load Order[/b] preview based on available package information and reviewed knowledge.

You review the changes before applying them.

Applying a preview creates an unsaved, undoable edit. It does not automatically save or sync the result.

[b]The Advisor is not a universal compatibility solver.[/b] Always follow mod-author instructions when available.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/09-themes-and-personalization.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Redux includes three built-in themes:

[list]
[*][b]Redux Dark[/b][/*]
[*][b]Redux Light[/b][/*]
[*][b]Parchment[/b][/*]
[/list]

Custom themes can be built with live color editing.

Other options include imported fonts, PNG category icons, multiple text sizes, Reduce Motion, configurable keyboard shortcuts, icon and label visibility controls, background effects, and other appearance settings.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/10-installation.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

[b]Portable ZIP[/b]

Download the Redux ZIP from the Files tab, extract the complete archive into its own writable folder, and launch:

[b]Redux.exe[/b]

Do not run Redux from inside the ZIP or place it inside the Baldur's Gate 3 installation directory. A dedicated folder such as [b]C:\Modding\Redux[/b] is recommended.

Redux can notify you when an update is available and apply supported updates in place. To update manually, close Redux and extract the complete new archive over your existing Redux folder.

Redux does not use an installer. To remove it, close Redux, keep any settings or backups you still need, and delete its folder. Removing Redux does not remove your mods, saves, Script Extender, or game-directory mods.

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/INSTALLATION.md][b]Full Installation, Update, Rollback & Removal Guide[/b][/url]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/11-requirements.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or Windows 11, x64[/*]
[*].NET 8 Desktop Runtime[/*]
[*]Baldur's Gate 3[/*]
[/list]

Linux, macOS, Wine, and Proton are not currently supported.


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/12-privacy.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Redux is a local desktop application.

There is no Redux account, advertising, analytics, or general-purpose telemetry. Redux does not upload your mod list, saves, categories, notes, settings, or diagnostics to a Redux service.

Optional online features only make network requests when enabled or used.

[color=#E26473][b]Never share API keys, credentials, signed download URLs, or screenshots containing them.[/b][/color]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/13-bugs-feedback-and-support.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Public testing is especially useful because it exposes Redux to mod setups and system configurations I cannot reproduce on my own.

If something breaks, please report it.

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/issues][b]GitHub Issues[/b][/url] — reproducible bugs and focused feature requests.

[url=https://discord.gg/rJJF89vqFZ][b]Redux Discord[/b][/url] — troubleshooting, discussion, testing feedback, and quicker back-and-forth when narrowing down a problem.

For bug reports, reproduction steps, screenshots, Windows scaling, and relevant mod information are much more useful than a general description that something is broken.

[color=#E26473][b]Do not post API keys, signed URLs, credentials, private notes, complete saves, or unreviewed logs.[/b][/color]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/14-credits.png?v=3275e4e[/img][/center]

Redux is built on [url=https://github.com/LaughingLeader/BG3ModManager][b]LaughingLeader's BG3 Mod Manager[/b][/url] and retains substantial upstream code and behavior.

It also uses [b]Norbyte's LSLib[/b] along with a number of other open-source libraries, fonts, accessibility components, and icon resources.

